WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.410
Zack Snyder's new film "Army of the Dead"
follows an elite team hired to steal millions

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:10.430
of dollars from a vault beneath a Las Vegas
casino during a zombie outbreak.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:15.340
Unsurprisingly, Snyder's assembled a talented
group of actors to play this group of thieves.

00:00:15.340 --> 00:00:17.750
Here's where you've seen them before.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:23.341
Dave Bautista seems to be following in Dwayne
Johnson's footsteps, as the former WWE star

00:00:23.341 --> 00:00:26.420
has shown talent in both action and comedy
roles.

00:00:26.420 --> 00:00:31.170
Bautista has rapidly become quite the in-demand
commodity, and he appears to be the central

00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:36.190
star in "Army of the Dead", where he plays
Scott Ward, the leader of the heist group.

00:00:36.190 --> 00:00:41.180
Bautista is probably most recognizable as
Drax the Destroyer in the Marvel Cinematic

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.889
Universe, and he will reprise the role in
the upcoming "Guardians of the Galaxy Vol.

00:00:45.889 --> 00:00:46.889
3."

00:00:46.889 --> 00:00:51.549
Some of his other major starring roles also
blend action and comedy, such as "My Spy"

00:00:51.549 --> 00:00:52.549
and "Stuber."

00:00:52.549 --> 00:00:57.699
You may also have caught Bautista in an supporting
role in "Blade Runner 2049," and he's part

00:00:57.699 --> 00:01:01.850
of another big budget sci-fi flick — 2021's
"Dune."

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:07.450
Like many former WWE stars, Bautista also
occasionally returns to the ring for big ticket

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:12.100
events like Wrestlemania and Royal Rumble,
although he recently claimed to be retired

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:13.400
from the world of wrestling.

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.939
Even though she was born in 1996, Ella Purnell
has already been in Hollywood for over a decade.

00:01:19.939 --> 00:01:25.200
Her first credited role came in 2010, where
she played young Ruth in "Never Let Me Go,"

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:29.050
and she's gradually been building her portfolio
ever since.

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:34.030
In "Army of the Dead," she's playing the role
of Kate Ward, the estranged daughter of Bautista's

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:35.390
lead character.

00:01:35.390 --> 00:01:38.730
Some of Purnell's early work came in big-budget
blockbusters.

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:43.789
She played the young version of Angelina Jolie's
title character in "Maleficent" and she also

00:01:43.789 --> 00:01:46.750
popped up as Dolce in "Kick-Ass 2."

00:01:46.750 --> 00:01:52.119
Purnell was also part of the supporting ensemble
as Emma in "Miss Peregrine's Home for Peculiar

00:01:52.119 --> 00:01:57.009
Children," and she played a substantial role
in "Churchill" as Helen Garrett, secretary

00:01:57.009 --> 00:01:59.149
to the iconic prime minister.

00:01:59.149 --> 00:02:03.479
Purnell's star continues to shine, as she
recently wrapped a starring role on the television

00:02:03.479 --> 00:02:04.530
series "Sweetbitter."

00:02:05.770 --> 00:02:08.720
Omari Hardwick's first plan didn't involve
Hollywood.

00:02:08.720 --> 00:02:13.920
In fact, he was actually a starting defensive
back for the Georgia Bulldogs football team

00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:16.450
during the 1995 season.

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:21.030
Hardwick was teammates with NFL greats like
Champ Bailey and Hines Ward and even declared

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.550
for the draft, but he wasn't selected.

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:28.280
He played during a rough stretch for the Bulldogs,
as this was when the Southeastern Conference

00:02:28.280 --> 00:02:32.780
was still completely dominated by the likes
of Florida and Tennessee.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:37.170
Hardwick pivoted to acting after the draft,
and he's part of the central cast of "Army

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:42.550
of the Dead," playing Vanderohe, a mercenary
packing an intimidating rescue saw.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:46.160
Hardwick's acting career has showcased him
in a wide variety of roles.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:51.560
He plays the lead on the Starz series "Power,"
and has also starred in several major films.

00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:56.760
He played Marcus Williams in "Kick-Ass," Chopshop
Jay in "The A-Team," and Mr. Blank in the

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.500
absolutely wild "Sorry to Bother You."

00:02:59.500 --> 00:03:04.230
He's got a lot of range, so it will be interesting
to see what route his character takes in "Army

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:05.230
of the Dead."

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:11.650
One of the biggest stars in "Army of the Dead"
is Ana de la Reguera, who plays Cruz, Scott

00:03:11.650 --> 00:03:14.590
Ward's old buddy and a fantastic mechanic.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:20.510
She may not be a household name, but de la
Roguera is involved in all facets of media.

00:03:20.510 --> 00:03:25.570
She first started making some waves in Spanish-language
telenovelas, and she continues to work in

00:03:25.570 --> 00:03:28.570
major films and series as a bilingual actress.

00:03:28.570 --> 00:03:34.120
Her first major role in a Hollywood production
came in 2006's "Nacho Libre", where she played

00:03:34.120 --> 00:03:36.010
Sister Encarnación [eng-kahr-nah-SYAWN].

00:03:36.010 --> 00:03:40.750
She had minor roles in a few major films in
the following years, including the buddy comedy

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:44.270
"Cop Out" and the bizarre sci-fi mashup "Cowboys
&amp; Aliens."

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:46.980
However, she's made more of a mark in television.

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:51.980
In addition to guest roles and her telenovela
work, de la Reguera has appeared in series

00:03:51.980 --> 00:03:55.650
like "Narcos," "Eastbound &amp; Down," "Power,"
and "Goliath."

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:59.680
De la Reguera has also branched out a bit
into writing and producing.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:03.750
She's the creator of the Spanish-language
Comedy Central series "Ana," in which she

00:04:03.750 --> 00:04:05.120
also stars.

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:09.210
She's hosted events, acted on stage, and done
some serious modeling work.

00:04:09.210 --> 00:04:11.130
In other words, she's everywhere.

00:04:12.390 --> 00:04:17.010
German actor Matthias Schweighöfer hasn't
been a part of too many Hollywood productions,

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:20.470
but he's been pretty successful in German-language
film and television.

00:04:20.470 --> 00:04:24.380
He appears in "Army of the Dead" as Ludwig
Dieter [DEE-ter], an expert safecracker.

00:04:24.380 --> 00:04:28.980
Though most of Schweighöfer's work is German,
there are still a few places you may have

00:04:28.980 --> 00:04:30.810
caught him on the other side of the Atlantic.

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:36.580
He had a small role as another character named
Dieter in 2002's "Feardotcom," and he had

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:39.750
a very brief appearance in the Tom Cruise-led
"Valkyrie".

00:04:39.750 --> 00:04:43.610
A few of his German works have also gotten
some international attention.

00:04:43.610 --> 00:04:47.620
He starred in "The Red Baron" and "The Most
Beautiful Day," and he played in Amazon's

00:04:47.620 --> 00:04:51.090
first German-language original series, "You
Are Wanted."

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:53.840
He's also lent his voice to a few different
productions.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:58.600
For example, he voices the Fox in the German
dub of Netflix's "The Little Prince."

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:03.200
Schweighöfer is also directing and starring
in a prequel to "Army of the Dead," called

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:07.850
"Army of Thieves," which will release on Netflix
sometime after Zack Snyder's film.

00:05:08.850 --> 00:05:13.440
Actor Theo Rossi is one of the more recognizable
faces in the "Army of the Dead" cast, where

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:19.160
he plays Burt Cummings, a security guard who
isn't exactly the most upstanding or trustworthy

00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.160
guy.

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:24.170
Rossi has had large roles on a few different
popular television series and guest appearances

00:05:24.170 --> 00:05:25.810
on dozens of others.

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:30.490
Most of his film work to this point has been
minor, but he's shown up in a handful of recognizable

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:31.740
movies too.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:36.880
If Rossi looks familiar, it's probably from
one or two series where he played a big role.

00:05:36.880 --> 00:05:41.900
His breakout performance came on the FX series
"Sons of Anarchy," where he played Juan Carlos

00:05:41.900 --> 00:05:45.830
Ortiz, aka Juice, in more than 80 episodes.

00:05:45.830 --> 00:05:49.860
His other major television role was of the
streaming variety, where he played the villainous

00:05:49.860 --> 00:05:52.390
Shades Alvarez on Netflix's "Luke Cage."

00:05:52.390 --> 00:05:57.760
He's also had guest spots on series like "Veronica
Mars," "Lost," and "Grey's Anatomy," and he's

00:05:57.760 --> 00:06:00.600
appeared in films like "Cloverfield" and "Lowriders."

00:06:00.600 --> 00:06:04.410
Beyond his impressive acting, Rossi just seems
like a good dude.

00:06:04.410 --> 00:06:09.500
He supports several different nonprofit organizations,
including helping animals through the Humane

00:06:09.500 --> 00:06:14.260
Society, disaster victims through StatenStrong,
and veterans through Boot Campaign.

00:06:15.580 --> 00:06:20.919
Paris-born actress Nora Arnezeder plays Lilly,
also known as the Coyote, in "Army of the

00:06:20.919 --> 00:06:23.900
Dead," part of the mercenary crew involved
with the heist.

00:06:23.900 --> 00:06:28.861
Arnezeder only has a couple dozen roles to
her credit at this point in her career, but

00:06:28.861 --> 00:06:31.270
there are a few different films you may have
caught her in.

00:06:31.270 --> 00:06:36.270
Her first major exposure to American audiences
probably came in 2012's "Safe House," where

00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.120
she played the girlfriend of Ryan Reynolds'
character.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:44.370
That same year, she appeared alongside Elijah
Wood in the horror remake "Maniac" and starred

00:06:44.370 --> 00:06:49.900
with the likes of Bradley Cooper, Zoe Saldana,
and Olivia Wilde in "The Words."

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:54.710
Recently, Arnezeder's more recognizable work
comes from a few TV series.

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:59.210
She played Chloe in the first few seasons
of "Zoo" and Anna Maria on "Mozart in the

00:06:59.210 --> 00:07:00.210
Jungle."

00:07:01.210 --> 00:07:05.790
Veteran actor Hiroyuki Sanada has seamlessly
transitioned between Japanese and American

00:07:05.790 --> 00:07:08.030
cinema over his impressive career.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:12.060
His first credit came in 1965 at just five
years old!

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:16.100
Judging from what we've seen of "Army of the
Dead," his character, Bly Tanaka, looks to

00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.940
play a major part in the events that occur.

00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:23.350
After all, he's the casino boss who decides
to take advantage of the zombie mayhem and

00:07:23.350 --> 00:07:26.530
hire Dave Bautista to pull off an undead robbery.

00:07:26.530 --> 00:07:31.120
Fans of Japanese films might recognize Sanada
from "The Twilight Samurai," considered one

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:33.980
of Japan's best movies of the last few decades.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:39.699
The film won 12 awards from the Japanese Academy,
including all the big ones — Best Screenplay,

00:07:39.699 --> 00:07:43.030
Director, Film, and Actor for Sanada's role.

00:07:43.030 --> 00:07:47.190
And horror fans know that he also starred
in the original "Ringu".

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:51.290
Sanada has made appearances in films like
"Speed Racer," "The Wolverine," and "The Last

00:07:51.290 --> 00:07:52.290
Samurai."

00:07:52.290 --> 00:07:56.610
But he's also started to show up in major
blockbuster projects as of late.

00:07:56.610 --> 00:08:01.169
For example, he appeared in HBO's "Westworld,"
and had a small but memorable role as the

00:08:01.169 --> 00:08:03.979
mob boss killed by Hawkeye in "Avengers: Endgame."

00:08:03.979 --> 00:08:10.860
And in 2021, he told us all to "get over here"
when he played Hanzo Hasashi, aka Scorpion,

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:12.110
in "Mortal Kombat."

00:08:13.450 --> 00:08:18.160
Actress Tig Notaro is most famous as a stand-up
comedian, but she's had more than her fair

00:08:18.160 --> 00:08:21.620
share of recognizable roles in film and television.

00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:26.310
Interestingly, she was actually brought into
her role as Marianne Peters, the cigar-smoking

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:30.540
helicopter pilot, in "Army of the Dead" after
the film had already wrapped.

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:34.959
She filmed her scenes after the fact and was
digitally inserted into the movie, replacing

00:08:34.959 --> 00:08:39.680
actor Chris D'Elia after numerous disturbing
allegations emerged about him.

00:08:39.680 --> 00:08:43.620
Notaro's work as a stand-up comedian helped
her break into the mainstream, and the audio

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:48.310
of her incredible set "Live," in which she
discusses her cancer diagnosis, is the stuff

00:08:48.310 --> 00:08:49.559
of stand-up legend.

00:08:49.559 --> 00:08:53.329
There's even a Netflix documentary about the
set called "Tig."

00:08:53.329 --> 00:08:57.550
She's worked with a number of other comedians
on projects like "Inside Amy Schumer," "Lady

00:08:57.550 --> 00:08:59.439
Dynamite," and "The Jim Gaffigan Show."

00:08:59.439 --> 00:09:05.610
Plus, she created and starred in the semi-autobiographical
"One Mississippi," and more recently, she

00:09:05.610 --> 00:09:08.360
appeared as Jett Reno on "Star Trek: Discovery."

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:10.100
"Where the hell have you been?"

00:09:10.100 --> 00:09:15.720
"Realizing my lifelong dream of taking us
from plasma to fully polaric warp conduits."

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:22.010
Raúl Castillo is an actor of stage and screen
who appears in "Army of the Dead" as Mikey

00:09:22.010 --> 00:09:26.010
Guzman, a character who's being described
as a "go-for-broke influencer."

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:31.000
Castillo is also a well-regarded playwright
alongside his body of acting work.

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:35.199
In fact, Castillo has long been involved with
several theater companies and has appeared

00:09:35.199 --> 00:09:38.389
on stage several times, mainly with LAByrinth.

00:09:38.389 --> 00:09:42.320
Most of Castillo's acting roles have been
relatively small, though he's occasionally

00:09:42.320 --> 00:09:44.399
broken into something a bit bigger.

00:09:44.399 --> 00:09:49.550
He's probably best known for the HBO series
"Looking," where he played Richie Ventura.

00:09:49.550 --> 00:09:54.699
He's also had recurring roles on a few Netflix
series, playing Nick on "Atypical" and Felix

00:09:54.699 --> 00:09:55.999
on "Seven Seconds."

00:09:55.999 --> 00:10:00.740
He's appeared in guest roles on several other
television series, including "Riverdale" and

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:05.389
"Gotham," where he showed up as the Flamingo
during the "Rise of the Villains" season.

00:10:05.389 --> 00:10:09.519
Castillo has seen a bit of film work over
his career, but it's typically been small

00:10:09.519 --> 00:10:10.519
roles and indie features.

00:10:10.519 --> 00:10:15.160
Keep a sharp eye during "Knives Out" –- Castillo
plays a police officer in the background.

00:10:16.160 --> 00:10:21.110
Actor Garret Dillahunt plays Martin in "Army
of the Dead," the head of casino security,

00:10:21.110 --> 00:10:23.889
and he's had a long career in both film and
television.

00:10:23.889 --> 00:10:26.920
He's one of those classic "I know that guy!"
actors.

00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:30.800
You've almost certainly seen him in something
over the last several decades, even if you

00:10:30.800 --> 00:10:34.290
can't quite put a finger on where you recognize
him from.

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:38.279
Television is where Dillahunt has had the
most success, and he's proven himself extremely

00:10:38.279 --> 00:10:39.279
versatile.

00:10:39.279 --> 00:10:43.640
He played Burt Chance on the comedy "Raising
Hope," Jody Kimball-Kennedy on "The Mindy

00:10:43.640 --> 00:10:49.499
Project," Ty Walker on "Justified" and both
Jack McCall and Frances Wolcott on "Deadwood."

00:10:49.499 --> 00:10:52.490
That's just the tip of the iceberg for his
television work too.

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:57.529
On the film side of things, Dillahunt often
plays supporting roles in major movies, memorably

00:10:57.529 --> 00:11:02.199
showing up as a corrupt sheriff in "Winter's
Bone" and Tommy Lee Jones' young deputy in

00:11:02.199 --> 00:11:04.759
"No Country for Old Men."

00:11:05.759 --> 00:11:09.139
Michael Cassidy is one of those actors who
will probably always be known for his first

00:11:09.139 --> 00:11:10.139
role.

00:11:10.139 --> 00:11:14.529
He played Zach Stevens, the sometimes-boyfriend
to Summer Roberts on "The O.C."

00:11:14.529 --> 00:11:18.660
Even though he's appeared in dozens of other
roles since, that's the role that seems to

00:11:18.660 --> 00:11:19.910
be attached to him.

00:11:19.910 --> 00:11:23.839
Maybe his appearance as Sergeant Cassidy in
"Army of the Dead" will help him break free

00:11:23.839 --> 00:11:25.279
from his TV origins.

00:11:25.279 --> 00:11:29.680
Besides "The O.C.," Cassidy has appeared in
a number of other television roles.

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:34.180
He played Tyler Mitchell on the TBS series
"Men at Work," and he's had recurring roles

00:11:34.180 --> 00:11:37.540
on series like "The Magicians," "Smallville,"
and "Privileged."

00:11:37.540 --> 00:11:41.759
Speaking of "Smallville," that wasn't his
only dip into the DC swimming pool.

00:11:41.759 --> 00:11:46.709
Remember when it was revealed that Zack Snyder
killed off Jimmy Olsen in "Batman v. Superman"

00:11:46.709 --> 00:11:50.490
without even naming him and said that was
his way of having "fun with him?"

00:11:50.490 --> 00:11:52.560
Jimmy Olsen was played by Michael Cassidy!

00:11:53.560 --> 00:11:57.980
Samantha Win got started in Hollywood doing
stunt work, but she had her first traditional

00:11:57.980 --> 00:12:03.519
role in 2013 and has started to appear more
as an actress and less in her former occupation.

00:12:03.519 --> 00:12:08.720
In "Army of the Dead," she plays Chambers,
a character described as the "ride-or-die"

00:12:08.720 --> 00:12:14.029
to Raúl Castillo's influencer, and it's seemingly
her most high-profile role yet.

00:12:14.029 --> 00:12:18.489
Win has worked a lot with Zack Snyder in the
past, performing stunts on films like "Sucker

00:12:18.489 --> 00:12:19.809
Punch" and "Man of Steel."

00:12:19.809 --> 00:12:23.990
Win also appeared in "Man of Steel" in her
debut role as Car-Vex.

00:12:23.990 --> 00:12:29.350
She would make several more appearances in
the DC cinematic universe as one of the Amazonians.

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:33.689
Considering the success DC has had with "Wonder
Woman," it seems likely that Win will make

00:12:33.689 --> 00:12:38.029
another appearance in the Amazon spinoff that's
headed our way, even though she was killed

00:12:38.029 --> 00:12:40.209
during the events of "Justice League."

00:12:40.209 --> 00:12:44.819
She's also utilized her martial arts talents
doing motion capture work for video games

00:12:44.819 --> 00:12:49.910
like "Call of Duty: Advanced Warfare" and
appearing as Kitana in the web series "Mortal

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:50.910
Kombat: Legacy."

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:56.529
"Army of the Dead" has a pretty impressive
collection of multinational actors, and Huma

00:12:56.529 --> 00:13:00.899
Qureshi is one that might not ring a lot of
bells to Western audiences.

00:13:00.899 --> 00:13:05.929
She plays Geeta in the film, a mom who's gone
missing in the zombie-infested danger zone

00:13:05.929 --> 00:13:07.389
that is Las Vegas.

00:13:07.389 --> 00:13:12.319
Qureshi was born in India, and she's found
a ton of success in Hindi-language films.

00:13:12.319 --> 00:13:14.860
Her first major role drew a lot of attention.

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:20.339
Her portrayal of Mohsina in "Gangs of Wasseypur"
saw her nominated for several awards, as did

00:13:20.339 --> 00:13:23.000
her role in "Dedh Ishqiya" a few years later.

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:28.260
On the English-language side of things, Qureshi
has only had a few notable appearances, such

00:13:28.260 --> 00:13:33.800
as her role alongside Hugh Bonneville and
Gillian Anderson in the historical drama "Viceroy's

00:13:33.800 --> 00:13:34.800
House."

00:13:34.800 --> 00:13:39.029
Qureshi also starred on a Hindi-language Netflix
series entitled "Leila."

00:13:39.029 --> 00:13:42.949
With the exposure she'll get from "Army of
the Dead," it seems likely we'll see more

00:13:42.949 --> 00:13:44.819
of her in future Hollywood projects.

00:13:44.819 --> 00:13:47.689
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:13:47.689 --> 00:13:51.339
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
actors are coming soon.

00:13:51.339 --> 00:13:54.930
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

